 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 518497,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Find the monthly payment for a $9,800.00 loan at a 13.8% interest for 4 years.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>The amount of monthly payments, <i>A</i>, for a loan with principal <i>P</i>, monthly simple interest rate <i>r</i> (in decimal form), for <i>t</i> number of months is found using the formula <span data-math=\"A = P \\times \\frac{{r \\times {{\\left( {1 + r} \\right)}^t}}}{{{{\\left( {1 + r} \\right)}^t} - 1}}\"></span>. The monthly interest rate is the annual interest rate divided by 12.</p>\n<p>4 years = 48 months</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"A = 9,800 \\times \\frac{{\\frac{{0.138}}{{12}} \\times {{\\left( {1 + \\frac{{0.138}}{{12}}} \\right)}^{48}}}}{{{{\\left( {1 + \\frac{{0.138}}{{12}}} \\right)}^{48}} - 1}} = \\$266.82\"></span></p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "$266.82"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
